issues.suggestedFix:
Make the service signature consistent with the problem statement, template, controller and tests: change PersonService.addParent to return Person and return the persisted entity. For example:

public Person addParent(Person person, Person parent) {
    if (person.getParents().size() >= 2) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "A person can only have 2 parents");
    }
    person.getParents().add(parent);
    return personRepository.save(person);
}

Alternatively, if the intended design is to keep a void return, update the problem statement, template method signature, PersonResource callers and all tests to reflect void (less recommended since callers and docs currently expect a returned Person).
